 "honest": [
  "a wider book is not a strategy change and not a better strategy: width is monotone in risk here, and this face only asks at which width the calendar question becomes answerable at all",
  "the draws are seeded and the seed list is published, so the same cutoff reproduces the same names; the sd per width is the draw distribution's own spread, not a confidence interval on returns",
  "draws_needed assumes draws are independent; correlated draws (the same month-end book recurring) would need more, so it is a floor",
  "where pool_binds is true the wide rung could not fill pick_n at some sessions, so that rung holds a narrower book than its label",
  "each rung is burned at cost x0 and no cost arm is re-derived; descriptive census only, no gate, no prereg, no trial count",
  "gap_is_width_invariant is the precondition for reading the ladder as one effect measured more finely: if the gap itself moves more than the tightest control's standard error between rungs, each rung is measuring a different quantity and a 'resolved' rung decides only that rung's number, not the narrow one"
 ],
